BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Totem Pole Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T163000
UID:6a85e74abe14820029887d15@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Truth and Reconciliation day is September 30th. On this day\,
  we honour Indigenous children who never returned home from Indian Residen
 tial Schools\, as well as Survivors of the Indian Residential School Syste
 m and their families. Wear your orange shirt in solidarity and create a cu
 stom Totem craft in the tradition of aboriginals who resided in the Pacifi
 c Northwest Coast of North America.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e74abe14820029887d15
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
