BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rabbit and Bear Paws Puppet Show: The Way
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T150000
UID:6a6a28cd898f0d2051150ca2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For Children up to age 12 with their parent or caregiver.\nThi
 s interactive puppet show from Chad Solomon features characters from the R
 abbit and Bear Paws children's graphic novel series. In this performance\,
  audiences will experience the story of how the turtle carried our world o
 n her back\, and how the tiny muskrat succeeded in giving us the greatest 
 gift of all - a place to call home\, Turtle Island.\nChad Solomon\nis a me
 mber of the Henvey Inlet\, First Nation. His grandfather taught him that n
 o matter how old you become\, you should always be young-at-heart and that
  laughter is the greatest medicine. This is the spirit behind the comical 
 Adventures of Rabbit and Bear Paws series.\nDrop-in only. No Registration 
 Required.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a28cd898f0d2051150ca2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
