BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orange Shirt Day Storytime and Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T173000
UID:6a8f041d29a7dd0d6746c0b1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special reading of Phyllis’s Orange Shirt by P
 hyllis Webstad and When We Are Kind by Monique Gray Smith in honour of Ora
 nge Shirt Day. After the story time\, kids can get creative by making hear
 t crafts and decorating their own paper orange shirt to celebrate kindness
 \, caring and friendship\, and honour the truth that Every Child Matters.\
 nThis is a staff-led program using resources developed by The Orange Shirt
  Society.\nFor kids ages 4-8 with a parent or caregiver.\nIf you or your c
 hild lives with a disability\, and requires an accessibility accommodation
  to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Service by 
 email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca\nor voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a 
 request. Please contact at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f041d29a7dd0d6746c0b1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T153000
UID:6a8dd9b957c264087ad3ab59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Parkdale branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety
  of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the na
 tural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differen
 t species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nT
 he tour will start and end at the Parkdale branch in the branch lobby area
  and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. This pro
 gram takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\,
  registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThere may be uneven
 \, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly 
 for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\,
  comfortable shoes).\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/ca
 regiver. Registration is required.
LOCATION:Parkdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dd9b957c264087ad3ab59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
