BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orange Shirt Day Storytime and Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T140000
UID:6a7b5d684c610f0038947437@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special reading of\nPhyllis's Orange Shirt\nby P
 hyllis Webstad and\nWhen We Are Kind\nby Monique Gray Smith in honour of O
 range Shirt Day. After the storytime\, kids can get creative by making he
 art crafts and decorating their own paper orange shirt to celebrate kindn
 ess\, caring and friendship\, and honour the truth that Every Child Matte
 rs.\nFor kids ages 4-8 with a parent or caregiver.\nThis is a staff-led pr
 ogram using resources developed by The Orange Shirt Society.\nPlease regis
 ter each participant. Drop-ins are welcome while supplies last.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event an
 d program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the
  library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at 
 answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b5d684c610f0038947437
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
