BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tech Activity Zone for Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T120000
UID:6a904a55be148200298a6e4e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun experimenting with a variety of tech and hands-on act
 ivities designed for\nchildren ages 4-12\n. Take on STEAM challenges with 
 Keva planks and Feltro\, learn coding basics with Dash and Sphero robots\,
  explore AI using a silly story and song generator\, and more!\n***\nAbout
  this event\nDigital Expo 2026 is a dynamic day of learning\, exploration 
 and connection focused on shaping a responsible AI future for everyone.\nF
 eaturing inspiring speakers and interactive exhibits\, as well as hands-on
  workshops for adults\, kids and teens\, the event explores how emerging t
 echnologies are transforming our lives\, communities and civic institution
 s.\nTogether\, we'll examine the opportunities and challenges of AI to fos
 ter a more informed\, inclusive and empowered digital society that protect
 s Canadians and safeguards democracy.\nCheck out tpl.ca/digitalexpo for mo
 re information about the Expo and the workshops.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Novella Room\, 2nd Floor (Appel Salon
 )
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904a55be148200298a6e4e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
